### Q5 — Rank customers by total amount spent, highest first
*(Window function: RANK)*

```sql
WITH customer_totals AS (
  SELECT c.customer_id, c.customer_name,
         SUM(oi.quantity * p.price) AS total_spent
  FROM customers c
  JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id
  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id
  JOIN products p ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
  GROUP BY c.customer_id, c.customer_name
)
SELECT customer_name, total_spent,
       RANK() OVER (ORDER BY total_spent DESC) AS spend_rank
FROM customer_totals
ORDER BY spend_rank;
```

**What it answers:** A leaderboard of customer value — `RANK()` assigns a position to every customer by total spend, useful for loyalty programs or targeted promotions.

