### Q6 — Number each customer's orders in the order they were placed
*(Window function: ROW_NUMBER, partitioned by customer)*

```sql
SELECT c.customer_name, o.order_id, o.order_date,
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY c.customer_id ORDER BY o.order_date) AS order_seq
FROM orders o
JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
ORDER BY c.customer_name, order_seq;
```

**What it answers:** Tracks each customer's order history as a numbered sequence (1st order, 2nd order, 3rd order...) — useful for identifying first-time vs. repeat buyers.

