### Q7 — Running total of revenue over time, ordered by order date
*(Window function: SUM ... OVER, ordered)*

```sql
WITH order_revenue AS (
  SELECT o.order_id, o.order_date,
         SUM(oi.quantity * p.price) AS order_total
  FROM orders o
  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id
  JOIN products p ON p.product_id = oi.product_id
  GROUP BY o.order_id, o.order_date
)
SELECT order_id, order_date, order_total,
       SUM(order_total) OVER (ORDER BY order_date, order_id) AS running_total
FROM order_revenue
ORDER BY order_date, order_id;
```

**What it answers:** Shows cumulative revenue growth day by day — the kind of chart management would use to see whether sales are accelerating.

